# EVERY WITHDRAWAL RULE IS WRITTEN IN BOTH FORMS, AND HERE IS WHY.
#
# Until 18 Aug 2026 all nine of them named only the .html address, while the
# site canonicalises extensionless — /x.html 307s to /x, and the sitemap and
# every canonical tag name the extensionless form. So a withdrawn page had a
# working old URL and a dead one, and the dead one was the shape a reader would
# have got from search or from a shared canonical link. All nine extensionless
# forms were measured 404 on the live site that day.
#
# A redirect that only catches the form nobody links is not a redirect. From
# here: withdraw a page, write both lines.
#
# The campaign plate was withdrawn. It had been published and indexed, so send
# its old URL to the dungeon index rather than leaving a dead end.
/dungeons/campaign-10-to-50.html  /dungeons/index.html  301
/dungeons/campaign-10-to-50       /dungeons/index.html  301

# Our own Plane of Sky tracker was withdrawn on 17 Aug 2026 and replaced by Sky
